       "@type": "belief",
       "@id": "copies/xx912rs1788.jsonld#date-belief",
       "certainty": "true",
       "reasons": [
        {
         "@type": "meaningComprehension",
         "comprehends": [
          "copies/xx912rs1788.jsonld#inscription-text"
         ],
         "note": "Ink, one line on the lower (upright) panel, in the order number, date, initials. The three pairs of the date are each plain, 12 and 11 as parallel strokes and 10 as a 1 beside an oval. Two reservations that do not touch the date: the second figure of the roll number has a flat top stroke over a single bowl and could be read 5, giving 1546 instead of 1346; and the initials at the end are three letters closed by a point, whose capital could be H or K, so Hst. is the best I can make of them."
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
